            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0395" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15Franco–British/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-02T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>180. I received yesterday from the British Embassy a communication from Sir
                    Austen Chamberlain embodying the understanding reached between Great Britain and
                    France in relation to naval limitation, with the added suggestion that it should
                    be adopted as a basis for discussion by the Preparatory Conference. I have asked
                    the Embassy for the explanation of certain points which I do not fully
                    understand as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows substance of the note of August 2, 1928, to the British Chargé,
                    printed on <ref target="#pg266">page 266</ref>.]</p>
                <p>[Paraphrase.] I think it might be well for you to see Chamberlain and discuss
                    with him the various points covered by my inquiry. He will undoubtedly provide
                    you with a copy of the agreement, should you not already have seen it, and I
                    think you might be able through conversation to have more light thrown on the
                    subject than I shall get in writing from the Embassy here. [End paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
